<title>UK: Fountain Forestry to seek AIM listing.</title>
<headline>Fountain Forestry to seek AIM listing.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Fountain Forestry Plc, a provider of forest management and tree related services in the U.K. and U.S., said on Monday it planned to list on the London Stock Exchange's Alternative Investment Market (AIM) via a placing.</p>
<p>&quot;Fountain Forestry is seeking an AIM listing to help fund the continued expansion of the group,&quot; said chairman and chief executive Barry Gamble in a statement.</p>
<p>The adviser to the issue is Coopers &amp; Lybrand and the broker is Charles Stanley.</p>
<p>-- John Sutherland, London Newsroom +44 171 542 7945</p>
